  "tier": "told-once",
  "plain": "In the 2000s, a senior official at the NSA, the US agency that intercepts communications, stopped a team from telling President Bush about something they had discovered, saying \"Nope, I'm not going to let you do that.\" Eric Haseltine, a former NSA official, tells Michels this from his own time there, as an example of how findings can be kept from reaching the very top."
